        <senderName>Environment Canada</senderName>
        <headline>red warning - tornado - in effect</headline>
        <description>
At 11:38 a.m. CST, a severe thunderstorm capable of producing a tornado, is located over Serath. This severe thunderstorm is moving north at 35 km/h. Destructive winds, damaging hail and flooding rainfall are possible.

Locations and nearby areas that could be impacted include: Serath


###

This is a very dangerous and potentially life-threatening situation.

Tornado warnings are issued when a thunderstorm is producing or is likely to produce a tornado.

Tornadoes can be wrapped in rain and may not be visible.
</description>
        <instruction>Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</instruction>
        <web>https://weather.gc.ca/</web>
