        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 11:40 a.m. Central Standard Time Sunday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for South Central and Southeastern Saskatchewan. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: Lanigan, Jansen, Semans, Duval, Govan, Nokomis, Strasbourg, Rowans Ravine Park, Earl Grey, Silton, Lumsden, Regina Beach, Craven, Wynyard, Elfros, Foam Lake, Ituna, Lestock, Wishart, Punnichy and Raymore. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds and large hail are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
        </parameter>
